+**Looking a marker up (#2081).** A scheduled job that keeps a tracking issue finds it with `.github/scripts/find-marker-issue.mjs --repo "$REPO" --marker "$MARKER"`, which lists open issues and matches the marker as the whole of line 1. A comment lookup anchors on line 1 with jq `startswith` or Actions `startsWith`. Flag as a Blocker any `gh ... --search "... in:body"` (the search index strips HTML comments, so it silently matched nothing, #1919) and any unanchored `contains()` on a body (it matches anything that quotes the marker, which is how `qa-drift-check` overwrote and closed #1997). `npm run lint:marker-lookups` enforces both; an exemption belongs in that script's `ALLOWLIST` with a reason, not in the YAML.

